
PLACEMENT layer FIRED (ADR-028).

This turn carries no placement — the work has no address.
Emit the PLACEMENT block as literal text, then write
.claude/placement-registered via the Write tool:

  PLACEMENT: D0 > D3 <name> > D3.D2 <name> | "<charter title>"

Expand to the full ancestor tree ONLY if a Domain or Charter was minted.
Never block on a missing domain — mint under the deepest matching
ancestor and continue. The system decides the taxonomy, not the operator.

If intentional (one-shot): echo reason > .claude/placement-ack
(or PLACEMENT_DISABLED=1 / touch .claude/placement-disabled)

